# Full Audit Command

When the user says **"run full audit"** or **"run all audits"** or **"full audit"**:

## What to do

1. Run all **13** audit lanes (Code, Math, Feature/UX, **Mobile experience**, Security, Performance-Cost, Reliability-Ops, Data-Integrity, Business-Valuation, Growth-Funnel, Documentation, Legal-Compliance, Agent-Governance) following their respective process docs.
2. Write each report to `docs/audits/<lane>/YYYY-MM-DD-*-audit.md` (use today's date). **Exception:** Mobile experience uses `docs/audits/feature/YYYY-MM-DD-mobile-experience-audit.md` (see `docs/process/mobile-experience-audit-process.md`).
3. After all reports are written, run the **synthesis pass** per `docs/process/full-audit-synthesis.md`.
4. Write synthesis output to `docs/audits/synthesis/YYYY-MM-DD-audit-synthesis.md`.
5. Audit only. Do not make code changes.
6. After completion, summarize top findings and report locations. Point the user to the synthesis file for PM review and task promotion.

## References

- Synthesis process: `docs/process/full-audit-synthesis.md`
- Lane processes: `docs/process/*-audit*.md` and `docs/process/*-audit-process.md` (Mobile experience also uses `docs/qa/mobile-experience-audit.md` for criteria)
- Audit index: `docs/audits/README.md`
